Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-03-2001||08:46 AM||||Checkout <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  they make a box for the front compartment to hold a 12" sub and <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  he make a complete center console that holdt a single 10" I plan on useing both by next year some time and useing Kicker XPL subs and a US amps VLX-50 to run them 25watt X 2 (cheater amp) I would guess that the single 10" in the center console would be better for sound Q with a high quality speaker like a Image Dynamics sub or a Eclipse 88000 alu. cone speaker but I don't know how deep either box is yet, and I can't wait to figure it all out but this all wait until I get a big 6-cyl in the car and running first. Hope I was some help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-03-2001||08:54 AM||||The sub box in the pic is made by AusFiero.  I had one until I decided to redo my interior.  Now it won't fit with my plans.  I had a 10" Cerwin Vega sub in the box (just like that but without the CD holder).  It would blow your ears out!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  If you plan on staying with the stock interior, I think that's one of the best ways to go.||||reg||1
